WEBVTT

00:01.320 --> 00:03.690
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:03.690 --> 00:06.610
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.610 --> 00:08.950
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:09.290 --> 00:12.650
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.650 --> 00:15.380
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.380 --> 00:18.530
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:18.530 --> 00:23.960
In the 31st year of Seika, a wild monkey plunged herself into the middle of that conflict.

00:23.960 --> 00:25.740
I'm a human!

00:25.740 --> 00:27.000
A girl!

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:49.560 --> 01:54.010
Situation 08

01:49.560 --> 01:54.010
Tezuka Sathoshi's
Schemes

01:54.820 --> 01:57.970
State your name and position.

01:58.400 --> 02:04.030
I'm Kasahara Iku, from the Kanto Library Defense Force, Library Task Force, Librarian First Class.

02:04.030 --> 02:07.150
Why did he name Kasahara?

02:07.150 --> 02:13.020
Even if we wanted to ask him, Sunagawa is faking an illness and staying home.

02:13.490 --> 02:18.330
He was probably led to her name during his interrogation.

02:18.330 --> 02:19.620
Led to me?

02:19.820 --> 02:21.690
You mean by Governmentalists?

02:22.800 --> 02:25.070
What? Governmentalists?

02:25.070 --> 02:26.430
Listen carefully, Kasahara.

02:26.430 --> 02:30.390
In the Library Force, we have two major parties.

02:30.390 --> 02:36.130
The Fundamentalists, lead by Commander Inamine, who value the independence and principles of libraries,

02:36.130 --> 02:40.940
and the Governmentalists, who hope to put libraries under the control of the government.

02:40.940 --> 02:46.860
The Governmentalists want to make the Fundamentalists look bad with this incident.

02:46.860 --> 02:50.240
But why are we...

02:50.240 --> 02:53.450
The Task Force is under the direct command of Commander Inamine.

02:54.500 --> 02:57.680
Any of our wrongdoings will also hurt Commander Inamine.

02:57.680 --> 03:03.770
They probably want to turn the tables on Commander Inamine, right along with the rest of the Fundamentalists.

03:06.050 --> 03:14.210
Looking at your record makes me think that many of your problems stem from actions based on Fundamentalist ideas.

03:15.270 --> 03:16.290
What's this?

03:16.290 --> 03:19.460
It's the interrogation prep course we made.

03:19.830 --> 03:22.750
Go over it thoroughly before the interrogation.

03:23.080 --> 03:26.390
A person like you must memorize it from start to finish.

03:26.390 --> 03:27.440
Write them out 100 times.

03:31.460 --> 03:39.080
In the past, another member of the Fundamentalists used the Right of Book Selection without proper permission.

03:40.200 --> 03:42.190
Just like you did.

03:42.190 --> 03:43.540
Is that...

03:43.540 --> 03:46.710
Let's get to our main point.

03:46.710 --> 03:50.630
You are aware of the incident involving LFC Sunagawa, correct?

03:51.020 --> 03:53.700
That topic came up during the talk with my team,

03:53.700 --> 03:55.350
so I'm aware of it.

03:55.350 --> 04:00.810
Have you had any special involvement with LFC Sunagawa in the past?

04:00.810 --> 04:03.610
We talked when we met,

04:03.610 --> 04:06.280
but I never thought about him too much.

04:06.280 --> 04:12.240
The day LFC Sunagawa performed the illegal book burning was February 18th.

04:12.690 --> 04:13.700
What?

04:13.700 --> 04:17.910
He packaged the hidden books in the storage area of the Second Browsing Area,

04:17.910 --> 04:20.750
and then carried them to the Third Public Building.

04:20.750 --> 04:25.000
He testified that LFC Kasahara assisted in this work.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.130
Is that a true statement?

04:29.170 --> 04:30.170
Those boxes!

04:32.540 --> 04:34.560
Looks like you know something.

04:34.560 --> 04:35.750
No.

04:35.750 --> 04:39.730
I helped him carry boxes, but I was not aware of the contents.

04:39.730 --> 04:43.940
LFC Sunagawa also testified that there was a verbal argument between you and him.

04:43.940 --> 04:48.250
It was regarding the Scorching Review that LFC Sunagawa was writing.

04:48.250 --> 04:53.840
I had thought it was an inappropriate piece to be part of the Library's services, so I pointed it out that day.

04:53.840 --> 04:59.250
So you two disagreed on the topic of the purpose of the Library. Is that correct?

04:59.250 --> 05:00.220
Shoot!

05:00.700 --> 05:03.390
You could put it that way.

05:03.390 --> 05:09.220
You stated earlier that you never thought too much about him.

05:09.220 --> 05:14.390
However, your last statement suggests that you had recognized him from before.

05:14.390 --> 05:15.890
Dang it!

05:16.370 --> 05:19.980
It was only after the Scorching Review became problematic.

05:19.980 --> 05:21.050
Nothing before...

05:21.050 --> 05:25.150
Then did you lie when you said you only talked when you met?

05:25.570 --> 05:27.260
It wasn't a lie!

05:27.260 --> 05:29.980
I didn't really mean "nothing."

05:30.920 --> 05:35.020
Shoot, I can't go on for much longer.

05:36.310 --> 05:37.480
Excuse me.

05:39.410 --> 05:43.740
Your time is up, so I'm taking LFC Kasahara back to her duties.

05:44.250 --> 05:45.870
Kasahara, come with me.

05:48.900 --> 05:50.460
You're back!

05:50.460 --> 05:52.510
Now, give it to me.

05:52.510 --> 05:57.050
Um, is it okay to have something like this during an interrogation?

05:57.050 --> 05:58.690
Are you kidding me?

05:58.690 --> 06:05.140
You incidentally had a personal item in your pocket, and the record button got pushed at the wrong moment. That's all.

06:05.140 --> 06:09.920
He packaged the hidden books in the storage area of the Second Browsing Area, and then carried them to the Third Public Building.

06:09.920 --> 06:13.290
He testified that LFC Kasahara assisted in that work.

06:11.440 --> 06:13.290
It's about that day!

06:13.290 --> 06:15.300
Is that a true statement?

06:13.810 --> 06:15.300
I was with them too.

06:15.300 --> 06:16.200
But...

06:16.860 --> 06:19.910
Why didn't he name me?

06:22.660 --> 06:23.900
Please excuse us.

06:24.690 --> 06:26.330
That was scary!

06:26.330 --> 06:27.920
Good job hanging in there.

06:27.920 --> 06:30.420
Don't be kind to me now!

06:30.420 --> 06:31.520
I'm close to tears.

06:32.430 --> 06:33.740
You can cry.

06:34.350 --> 06:37.140
Oh man, this is super-ultra cheesy.

06:37.140 --> 06:38.860
You idiot!

06:38.860 --> 06:40.400
Why didn't you turn it off?!

06:40.400 --> 06:42.600
This is a lot different from what you told me.

06:42.600 --> 06:44.520
I was caught by surprise too.

06:44.520 --> 06:47.940
I thought that news report was a scoop the reporter got on his own.

06:47.940 --> 06:50.260
You're saying you weren't aware?

06:52.040 --> 06:53.280
I'm sorry.

06:53.280 --> 06:55.380
No need to apologize.

06:55.380 --> 06:57.510
I wasn't counting on you that much anyway.

07:02.160 --> 07:04.530
I'm exhausted.

07:04.530 --> 07:09.500
I wonder if my Prince went through any interrogations after he saved me?

07:09.500 --> 07:13.570
It'd be sad if he went through anything like this because of me.

07:13.570 --> 07:16.670
Do you regret that you selected that book?

07:16.670 --> 07:17.890
I don't!

07:17.890 --> 07:20.560
If you don't, the same goes for him.

07:21.680 --> 07:23.140
Kasahara,

07:24.870 --> 07:27.000
things will get tough from now on.

07:28.880 --> 07:32.720
Promise me that you'll tell me if it gets hard to bear.

07:34.400 --> 07:35.360
Your answer?!

07:35.360 --> 07:36.650
Yes, Sir!

07:40.010 --> 07:41.370
Welcome back.

07:41.370 --> 07:42.780
Shibasaki?

07:42.780 --> 07:44.230
What's going on?

07:44.230 --> 07:45.660
Please take care of the rest.

07:45.660 --> 07:47.070
Of course.

07:47.070 --> 07:48.460
Now then, let's go get supper.

07:48.460 --> 07:50.450
Ah, yeah.

07:52.120 --> 07:53.880
And then...

07:57.880 --> 07:59.540
Act normal.

08:06.520 --> 08:07.730
Did you hear?

08:07.730 --> 08:09.050
Yeah, I did!

08:09.050 --> 08:11.050
Things will get tough from now on.

08:13.810 --> 08:15.770
What do you want to talk about?

08:17.070 --> 08:20.290
Was Sunagawa a member of the Future Library Project?

08:21.730 --> 08:22.950
What about it?

08:22.950 --> 08:27.950
I won't ignore it if your brother is involved in Kasahara's case.

08:30.260 --> 08:32.460
Tell me if you know anything.

08:33.670 --> 08:36.770
This is my problem.

08:36.770 --> 08:39.000
It's Kasahara's problem!

08:39.000 --> 08:41.040
Who else are you trying to protect?

08:45.600 --> 08:49.180
To be honest, this goes deeper than I thought.

08:50.730 --> 08:55.230
Anyway, it's not something you can handle by yourself.

08:55.590 --> 08:56.980
I know!

09:01.590 --> 09:04.730
I'm the reason Kasahara was targeted.

09:06.060 --> 09:13.860
I have an older brother who wants me to join his own group, the Future Library Project.

09:13.860 --> 09:20.580
But our philosophical beliefs are in conflict, so I declined his offer.

09:20.580 --> 09:23.760
He's trying to get at me from my surroundings.

09:23.760 --> 09:25.330
Hold it.

09:25.330 --> 09:29.900
That's a really out-there talk, coming from you.

09:29.900 --> 09:32.260
He's the kind of person who would do that.

09:36.010 --> 09:37.470
All right.

09:37.470 --> 09:39.690
I'll let the Captain know.

09:51.550 --> 09:55.330
I asked Commander Inamine to help us with the investigation,

09:55.330 --> 09:58.740
but we are trying to prove something that is as of yet without proof.

09:59.380 --> 10:01.800
We can't make any careless moves for now.

10:03.050 --> 10:09.630
Kasahara from Room 205, you have an incoming call. Please come to the Resident Director's room.

10:14.270 --> 10:17.140
Hello. Thank you for waiting.

10:17.140 --> 10:18.670
This is Kasahara speaking.

10:18.670 --> 10:20.190
Hello.

10:20.190 --> 10:23.360
Thank you for taking care of my brother.

10:34.040 --> 10:35.460
Instructor Dojo!

10:35.460 --> 10:38.940
Please gather Captain Genda and the rest of the team right away.

10:40.920 --> 10:42.900
This is the note Kasahara left behind.

10:42.900 --> 10:46.700
This means the Future Library Project is making its move, right?

10:46.700 --> 10:48.590
Where did you hear that?!

10:48.590 --> 10:51.560
Forget about that. What are you going to do about Kasahara now?

10:54.410 --> 10:56.410
I'll leave the rest to you.

10:59.210 --> 11:02.320
I know which restaurant he might be using.

11:02.320 --> 11:03.040
I...

11:03.040 --> 11:04.520
You stay here.

11:04.520 --> 11:07.320
He'll really have his way if you go now.

11:07.320 --> 11:09.870
But if I join the Future Library Project...

11:09.870 --> 11:13.540
Any actions allowing my subordinates to be given to the enemy are impermissible!

11:13.540 --> 11:14.870
But...

11:14.870 --> 11:16.470
Let's calm down.

11:16.470 --> 11:18.370
So, what should we do, Dojo?

11:20.980 --> 11:23.130
We'll wait for Kasahara to return.

11:23.130 --> 11:24.370
LOSC Dojo!

11:24.370 --> 11:29.800
What we think Tezuka Satoshi is trying to do is purely guesswork.

11:29.800 --> 11:33.640
If he's meeting Kasahara for the purpose of recruiting her to the research group,

11:33.640 --> 11:35.850
we have no right to interfere with his actions.

11:35.850 --> 11:36.560
But—

11:36.560 --> 11:38.020
Don't make me repeat myself!

11:44.860 --> 11:46.320
Was that okay?

11:46.320 --> 11:50.530
I might be thinking differently from you right now.

12:09.130 --> 12:14.720
Um, is it really okay to use such a nice place?

12:14.720 --> 12:16.550
It is.

12:16.550 --> 12:19.940
You're my brother's girlfriend, so I must treat you well.

12:23.400 --> 12:28.900
Don't you think it would be wonderful if there was no censorship?

12:31.010 --> 12:33.200
I do, of course!

12:33.980 --> 12:38.390
The Future Library Project is a research organization with the goal of making that possible.

12:38.390 --> 12:41.440
A world without censorship...

12:41.440 --> 12:44.040
It should be possible.

12:44.040 --> 12:48.920
In fact, there was no censorship until a little before you were born.

12:48.920 --> 12:50.160
Right...

12:50.160 --> 12:51.870
That's right!

12:51.870 --> 12:58.030
The Future Library Project is considering realistic measures to eliminate censorship from society.

12:58.030 --> 12:59.050
I wanna hear!

13:00.020 --> 13:01.740
Oh, I mean...

13:02.300 --> 13:03.480
I'd love to hear about it.

13:03.480 --> 13:10.450
The current Library Force system is not appropriate for fundamentally eliminating censorship.

13:10.450 --> 13:16.930
Don't you think the fact that the Media Cleansing Committee and the Library Force are fighting each other is wrong?

13:16.930 --> 13:17.980
Right...

13:17.980 --> 13:22.990
The fight that the Library Force puts up is nothing more than a response to the situation.

13:22.990 --> 13:26.460
Then what's the fundamental solution?

13:26.980 --> 13:30.120
It's for the Library to discard the Library Force system,

13:30.120 --> 13:35.180
and to be promoted to a state institution at the same level as the Media Cleansing Committee.

13:36.240 --> 13:38.180
Discard the Library Force?

13:38.180 --> 13:43.110
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

13:43.110 --> 13:44.760
Um...

13:45.660 --> 13:52.360
If that concept becomes a reality, how long would it take before censorship is gone?

13:53.980 --> 13:56.580
It'll be a long time.

13:56.580 --> 13:58.860
Ten or twenty years.

13:58.860 --> 14:00.790
But it's worth that time.

14:01.790 --> 14:03.640
Don't you think so?

14:06.640 --> 14:08.250
I can't do it.

14:08.250 --> 14:09.770
I can't wait for ten years.

14:10.750 --> 14:13.760
Because I want to read right now!

14:13.760 --> 14:19.610
I can't tell people to give up the freedoms they have now for a possible freedom they'll have several decades in the future.

14:19.610 --> 14:25.720
Besides, I admire that the Library Force fights to protect our current freedoms.

14:25.720 --> 14:28.700
I am proud to fight as a member of the Library Force.

14:28.700 --> 14:32.310
So I cannot agree with your idea.

14:34.740 --> 14:37.590
This is why I hate sensationalists.

14:37.590 --> 14:44.240
You overturn all the arguments with your feelings, no matter how diligently I explain things.

14:44.240 --> 14:47.400
All right, I'll play hardball too.

14:47.400 --> 14:52.120
To be honest, I don't care about you.

14:52.120 --> 14:54.420
The one I want is Hikaru.

14:55.210 --> 14:56.600
Tezuka?

14:56.600 --> 14:57.420
Yes.

14:57.420 --> 15:00.260
You were only my bait.

15:01.460 --> 15:04.980
Can you take a message to him?

15:04.980 --> 15:12.650
"If you join me, I'll stop the interrogations on Kasahara, prove her innocence, and set her free."

15:14.330 --> 15:20.060
I plotted everything from the beginning, including Sunagawa and the interrogations.

15:20.060 --> 15:23.270
It was all to strike this deal.

15:24.670 --> 15:25.870
That's cruel.

15:25.870 --> 15:28.820
I'm sorry about what I did to you.

15:28.820 --> 15:32.880
But I'm just that eager to get Hikaru.

15:33.540 --> 15:34.880
No...

15:35.380 --> 15:38.040
He's not being cruel to me.

15:39.520 --> 15:41.510
I can't take it.

15:42.640 --> 15:48.520
I can't take such a cruel message, when he's suffering from your evil scheme.

15:50.150 --> 15:54.150
Please stop hurting Tezuka!

16:00.450 --> 16:02.410
Who are you?

16:02.410 --> 16:05.120
I am Library Officer Second Class, Dojo Atsushi.

16:05.120 --> 16:06.600
She's my subordinate.

16:06.600 --> 16:07.660
I'm taking her back.

16:08.560 --> 16:09.580
Let's go.

16:12.570 --> 16:13.940
Oh, uh...

16:13.940 --> 16:15.930
Why are you in your uniform?

16:15.930 --> 16:16.700
Shut up!

16:16.700 --> 16:20.300
All of my suits are out being cleaned, so this was all I had left!

16:20.650 --> 16:24.620
Instructor Dojo, you're hurting my hand.

16:25.630 --> 16:30.260
I would have declined his offer and come back, even if you didn't come and get me.

16:31.150 --> 16:34.770
I only came to get you because I wanted to.

16:36.470 --> 16:40.830
You're going through a tough time, so I couldn't help but be worried about you.

16:40.830 --> 16:43.200
That's because I'm your superior officer.

16:43.200 --> 16:45.930
Man, that's not fair.

16:45.930 --> 16:47.410
If you treat...

16:48.390 --> 16:51.590
It wasn't called for.

16:51.590 --> 16:55.960
I promised you that I'd tell you if I couldn't bear it anymore.

16:58.890 --> 17:00.010
Good job hanging in there.

17:04.520 --> 17:05.800
Why...

17:05.800 --> 17:08.180
are you wearing high heels?

17:09.410 --> 17:16.270
After that, my interrogations regarding the illegal disposal of books ended abruptly,

17:16.270 --> 17:19.530
and I was once again presumed innocent for the time being.

17:19.530 --> 17:26.500
The way people in the dorm treat me is improving again because of Shibasaki's public relations work.

17:31.380 --> 17:32.580
Hi!

17:32.580 --> 17:34.870
You finally agreed to see me.

17:35.300 --> 17:36.870
This will be the last time.

17:36.870 --> 17:37.950
Never again.

17:39.050 --> 17:44.520
I don't come from a nice enough family to date a high-ranking officer of the DoJ.

17:46.810 --> 17:49.010
You know everything?

17:49.880 --> 17:55.250
You were doing everything as ordered by the Future Library Project, right?

17:55.250 --> 17:58.620
My ideal is the same as yours!

17:58.620 --> 18:02.350
Surprise attacks are not part of my ideal.

18:02.350 --> 18:03.630
Not against people on my side.

18:03.630 --> 18:06.630
I was against it!

18:06.630 --> 18:12.230
I was already in love with you by the time it happened.

18:14.020 --> 18:16.340
Can I apologize to you and...

18:16.340 --> 18:17.740
Please!

18:17.740 --> 18:20.330
This is a peaceful bargain.

18:20.330 --> 18:23.410
You really angered me.

18:37.380 --> 18:39.100
You can come out now.

18:40.860 --> 18:45.040
Sorry to make you be my guard.

18:45.040 --> 18:46.150
It's okay.

18:46.730 --> 18:50.790
Thanks for telling me about Asahina.

18:50.790 --> 18:52.410
You saved me.

18:52.410 --> 18:57.800
I just remembered seeing someone with the same name among my brother's acquaintances.

18:57.800 --> 19:01.020
Sorry for getting you involved.

19:01.020 --> 19:02.820
It's okay, I'm fine.

19:04.280 --> 19:07.180
I'll let you be alone now.

19:07.180 --> 19:08.160
Wait.

19:08.160 --> 19:11.060
Just so you know, I'm not that hurt.

19:11.060 --> 19:15.630
I can play the love game for my work without any hesitation.

19:15.630 --> 19:18.580
I think I'm really suited to being an informant.

19:19.350 --> 19:22.510
I think I could even sleep with a man, if that's what it took.

19:23.870 --> 19:26.290
I'll confess to something too.

19:26.290 --> 19:29.230
I have an inferiority complex regarding my brother.

19:29.230 --> 19:33.320
No matter how many times he disappoints me, I'm still expecting something from him.

19:34.200 --> 19:44.510
LOSC Dojo sort of resembles how my brother used to be when I admired him.

19:46.300 --> 19:48.810
Don't laugh!

19:48.810 --> 19:50.280
Sorry.

19:55.600 --> 19:58.080
Can you toss this for me?

19:58.950 --> 20:02.490
My brother gave it to me a long time ago.

20:02.490 --> 20:04.750
I can't bear to throw it out myself.

20:04.750 --> 20:05.940
Are you sure?

20:05.940 --> 20:06.830
Yeah.

20:10.280 --> 20:12.220
Do you want to go to a pawn shop with me?

20:13.070 --> 20:16.940
It'll give us enough to at least buy pick-me-up drinks.

20:16.940 --> 20:19.110
Hey! Are you going to pawn that off?!

20:19.110 --> 20:21.750
I know someone who'll buy it for a good price.

20:25.120 --> 20:27.510
Tezuka's brother!

20:29.140 --> 20:36.780
I was supposed to buy you dinner the other day, so please return the enclosed money to LOSC Dojo.

20:36.780 --> 20:44.910
I've learned to keep my hands off a girl who's had a heroic prince ever since her high school days.

20:44.910 --> 20:47.560
It's such a shame for me.

20:47.560 --> 20:49.280
Take care.

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
